  "notes": [
   "The booklet shows several small builds: the mini-doll Emma, a plant pot, a sun lounger with umbrella and goblet, and a splash pool with steps. They are separate models, so no joined edges link them.",
   "The minifigure (b1-b4) uses new part types for the hair, head, torso and legs. Their ports are my own choices.",
   "The sun lounger layering is ambiguous in the pictures. I assumed the 2x4 plate carries the pink 2x2 brick and the 2x6 plate overlaps it. The 2x6 plate carries the slope, the four tiles and the two feet.",
   "The pool step stacking is also ambiguous. I assumed two 2x2 white plates are stacked on the pink floor, with a 1x2 white plate beside them. Each carries one lime tile.",
   "The pool floor and wall assignments are approximate. The exact stud-to-stud pairings of the four pink curved plates, four aqua curved bricks and three trans-green windscreen panels are not clear from the pictures.",
   "Where a port is not in the catalogue entry, the port is left null: the soil plate underside, the goblet cup and the leaf centre stud.",
   "The set has 5 lime 1x2 tiles: 2 on the lounger and 3 on the pool steps. The set has 3 orange flowers: plant, goblet and umbrella. These are inferred from the inventory counts.",
   "Part type 4183133 (lime round plate 1x1, x2) is already in the catalogue and is used as the lounger feet."
  ]
